245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Manuel Clavel received his bachelor's degree in Philosophy from the Universidad de Navarra \(Spain\) in 1992, and his Ph.D from the same university in 1998. Currently, he is Senior Lecturer in Programming Languages and Methods at the Faculty of Engineering of Vietnamese-German University \(Binh Duong, Vietnam\). Previously, he was Associate Research Professor at the IMDEA Software Institute in Madrid \(Spain\), as well as Associate Professor at the Universidad Complutense de Madrid \(Spain\) and Visiting Professor at ETH Zurich \(Switzerland\). During his doctoral studies, he was International Fellow at the Computer Science Laboratory of SRI International \(1994-1997\) in California \(USA\) and a Visiting Scholar at the Computer Science Department of Stanford University \(1995-1997\). His research focuses on rigorous, tool-supported model-driven software development, including: modeling languages, model-driven security, model-driven privacy, model-driven code-generation, and model-driven automated-test generation. Related interests include specification languages, automated deduction, and theorem proving.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
