297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This research proposes a comprehensive solution for the recognition and digitization of Nom characters, an ancient Vietnamese writing system. The study leverages Ideographic Description Sequences \(IDS\) to address zero-shot and few-shot learning challenges in Nom character recognition. Our approach also apply the IDS representation for effective clustering and similarity-based search. The system includes automatic segmentation of Nom characters from documents using object detection and image segmentation models. Additionally, we develop a user-friendly web application for researchers to collect, preprocess, label, recognize, and query Nom character data. By integrating these components, our system aims to significantly advance the preservation and accessibility of Vietnam's valuable historical documents, while overcoming the limitations of current Nom digitization efforts that struggle with the vast diversity of characters and limited labeled datasets.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
